{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["He drew a bow — רובה קשת: one who draws a bow, and there are two conjugational patterns. וימררהו and רבו. And also יסבו, his Rabbis (?) — from the root רבב, like סובו from סבב, שומו שמים from שמם, דומו יושבי אי from דממה דקה — all of these are doubled in the final letter. But רובה is from the pattern of רבה. עשה. בנה. קנה. That is: עושה. בונה. קונה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text is garbled in places; translated hyper-literally as it stands. 'שני גזרות הן' is taken as referring to two conjugational patterns (binyanim), and the subsequent forms appear to illustrate different gemination patterns; the exact logic of the grammatical argument is textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:45.455200215Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}